// Longer product write-ups shown in the "About this product" section.
// Keyed by product id; applied over the catalog's details in products.ts.
export const productStories: Record<string, string> = {
  "76-dark-chocolate-bar-730593":
    "For dark chocolate lovers, this Italian bar has 76% cocoa for an intense, bittersweet flavor with deep roasted notes and a clean finish. Enjoy it a square at a time with a strong espresso, or set it on a cheese board next to aged cheese, toasted walnuts, and dried figs. It is also excellent for baking: chop it into cookies or melt it into a rich chocolate torta. Keep it in a cool, dry place.",
  "alfredo-sauce-730226":
    "A rich, creamy Alfredo-style sauce made in Italy, ready to warm and serve. Heat it gently in a saucepan and toss it with hot fettuccine for a classic, comforting bowl, finished with black pepper and a little chopped parsley. It is also delicious over gnocchi, stirred into a pan of sautéed mushrooms and spinach, or spooned over baked salmon. Warm it over low heat and stir often so it stays smooth.",
  "all-purpose-flour-2-2lb":
    "A fine, soft-wheat Type 00 flour milled in Italy and pre-sifted, so it is ready to measure and use. The silky texture makes it a true all-purpose flour: knead it into a smooth dough for homemade pasta, stretch it into a pizza base, or use it for cakes, cookies, and pastry. For an easy start, try fresh tagliatelle with just flour and eggs, rolled thin and cut by hand.",
  "apricot-fruit-spread-preserves":
    "A golden apricot spread with no high fructose corn syrup. It is soft and spreadable, with a bright, sunny apricot flavor. Spread it on warm toast or a croissant, swirl it into yogurt, or use it as a filling for crostata, thumbprint cookies, or rugelach. Warmed with a little water, it also makes a shiny glaze for fruit tarts or roast chicken.",
  "assorted-chocolate-truffles-gift-box":
    "A gift box of fifteen Italian chocolate truffles from Lombardy, with milk, dark, and hazelnut milk chocolate varieties so there is a favorite for everyone. Each truffle has a smooth chocolate shell and a soft, melting center. Bring it along to a holiday dinner, slip it into a gift basket, or open it after a family meal with a pot of coffee. It is an easy, elegant gift that looks as good as it tastes. Store in a cool, dry place.",
  "balsamic-glaze-modena":
    "Our balsamic glaze is slowly reduced from Balsamic Vinegar of Modena into a thick, glossy syrup with a rich sweet-and-tangy flavor. The squeeze bottle makes it easy to draw a neat line across a plate or a zigzag over a salad. Drizzle it on roasted chicken or vegetables, a caprese salad, grilled salmon, or slices of melon and fresh figs. It is even lovely over vanilla ice cream or a wedge of aged cheese. Store it in the pantry and shake before use.",
  "balsamic-vinegar-modena-500ml":
    "The same Balsamic Vinegar of Modena in a larger 500 ml bottle for kitchens that use it every day. Made in Modena, it has a deep color, a silky body, and a balanced sweet-tart flavor. Shake up a big jar of balsamic dressing for the week, marinate chicken or vegetables before grilling, or drizzle it over a caprese salad of tomatoes, basil, and fresh mozzarella. It also brightens roasted beets, sautéed onions, and fresh berries.",
  "balsamic-vinegar-modena-8oz":
    "Our Balsamic Vinegar of Modena is made in Modena, Italy, with a rich dark color and a balance of sweetness and tang. Whisk it with olive oil, salt, and pepper for a classic vinaigrette, splash it over roasted vegetables or grilled chicken, or add a spoonful to a mushroom risotto at the end. For a simple Italian dessert, sprinkle a few drops over fresh strawberries with a little sugar. The glass bottle keeps it fresh in the pantry.",
  "balsamic-vinegar-spray":
    "Balsamic Vinegar of Modena in a spray-top bottle, so you can mist a light, even coat over a salad instead of pouring. It is made in Modena from Italian grapes and has a rich, velvety balance of sweetness and acidity. Spritz it over mixed greens with a drizzle of olive oil, over grilled vegetables right off the heat, or across a platter of bruschetta just before serving. It is also a neat way to add a little shine to a finished plate.",
  "basil-pesto":
    "Our basil pesto blends fragrant basil into a smooth, bright green sauce that brings a taste of Liguria to the table in seconds. Toss a few spoonfuls with hot pasta and a splash of the cooking water to make it silky, spread it on a sandwich with tomatoes and mozzarella, swirl it into minestrone, or spoon it over grilled fish or potatoes. Keep the jar in the fridge once opened.",
  "bianca-white-thin-crust-pizza":
    "A white pizza, or pizza bianca, made without tomato sauce: a blend of cheeses and herbs on a thin, crisp crust. It is creamy, savory, and a nice change from the usual red pie. Bake it from frozen following the package directions until golden. Top the hot pizza with fresh arugula and a squeeze of lemon, or a drizzle of garlic olive oil and a pinch of black pepper.",
  "black-pepper-grinder":
    "Whole black peppercorns in a built-in grinder, so the pepper is ground fresh, right over your plate, with all its bold, aromatic heat. Twist to adjust from coarse to fine. Grind it generously over cacio e pepe, a bowl of pasta with olive oil, a steak, or a fresh salad, and finish soups and eggs with a few turns just before serving. Freshly ground pepper makes even simple food taste brighter.",
  "black-truffle-sauce":
    "Chopped black truffles and mushrooms are blended with olive oil into a rich, earthy, savory sauce. Toss a few spoonfuls with hot tagliatelle and a knob of butter, stir it into a risotto at the end, spread it on toasted crostini, or spoon it over a grilled steak. It also turns scrambled eggs into a special breakfast.",
  "blood-orange-juice":
    "Not made from concentrate, this juice has a deep ruby color and a sweet, tangy citrus flavor with a hint of berry. Shake the bottle before pouring and serve it well chilled. Enjoy a glass at breakfast with a warm croissant, mix it half and half with sparkling water for a quick spritz, or use it in a citrus salad dressing with olive oil and a pinch of salt. It also makes a beautiful red base for a holiday punch.",
  "breaded-eggplant-cutlets":
    "Tuscanini breaded eggplant cutlets, sliced eggplant in a golden coating, frozen and ready to cook whenever you need them. Bake or pan-fry them from frozen until hot and crisp, following the package directions. They make an easy eggplant parmigiana: layer them in a dish with tomato sauce and mozzarella and bake until bubbling. They are also delicious in a sandwich with fresh tomato and basil, or served on their own with a squeeze of lemon.",
  "breaded-mozzarella-sticks-730140":
    "Breaded mozzarella sticks made in Italy, with a crisp golden coating around warm, stretchy mozzarella. Bake or air-fry them from frozen following the package directions until golden and the cheese starts to ooze. Serve them hot with warm marinara for dipping. They are an easy appetizer for a party, a game night, or an after-school snack. Add a pinch of oregano or chili flakes to the sauce for extra flavor.",
  "breaded-mozzarella-sticks-family-pack-730141":
    "A family-size 15 oz pack of our breaded mozzarella sticks, with a crisp, golden coating and gooey melted mozzarella inside. Bake or air-fry them straight from frozen following the package directions. Pile them on a platter with a bowl of warm marinara or pizza sauce for dipping, and watch them disappear at parties, movie nights, and family dinners.",
  "bronze-cut-cavatappi-730604":
    "Cavatappi, the playful corkscrew-shaped tube, bronze cut for a textured surface that holds on to sauce. The hollow spirals fill up with creamy sauces, making them a favorite for baked mac and cheese. They are also great with pesto, a chunky tomato sauce, or tossed cold in a pasta salad. Cook in salted water until al dente. Finish with a generous handful of grated cheese.",
  "bronze-cut-farfalle-730605":
    "Farfalle, the bow-tie pasta, bronze cut for a slightly rough surface that holds sauce well. Their pinched centers stay pleasantly firm while the wings turn tender. Toss them with a light tomato sauce, pesto, or a creamy mushroom sauce, or cool them for a colorful pasta salad with cherry tomatoes, peas, mozzarella, and herbs. Cook in plenty of salted water until al dente.",
  "bronze-cut-pappardelle-730606":
    "Wide, generous ribbons of pappardelle, bronze cut for a slightly rough surface that grips hearty sauces. Pappardelle is the classic Tuscan pasta for slow-cooked ragù, and it is just as good with sautéed mushrooms and cream, or a rich braised beef sauce. Cook it in plenty of salted water until al dente and toss it straight into the sauce with a splash of pasta water.",
  "calabrian-chili-hot-pepper-jam":
    "A sweet-and-spicy jam made with Calabrian chili, balancing gentle sweetness with a warm, lingering heat. It is a natural for a cheese board: spoon it over fresh ricotta or a soft cheese on crostini, or serve it next to aged cheeses and crackers. It also makes a quick glaze for chicken wings, salmon, or roasted carrots, and a dab inside a grilled cheese sandwich is hard to beat.",
  "calabrian-chili-peppers":
    "Whole Calabrian chili peppers from southern Italy, long and bright red, preserved in olive oil. Calabrian chilies are known for their fruity, gently smoky flavor and a heat that ranges from medium to hot, and as they sit, the oil takes on their warmth too. Slice a pepper over pizza, stir one into a tomato sauce or a pan of garlicky greens, or tuck a few into a sandwich. Use the oil itself to drizzle over pasta or eggs.",
  "capers-in-brine":
    "Small, tangy Italian capers preserved in brine to keep their firm texture and bright, sharp flavor. A spoonful adds a salty, lemony pop to so many dishes: pasta puttanesca with tomatoes and olives, chicken piccata with lemon and butter, a niçoise-style salad with tuna and potatoes, or smoked salmon on a bagel. Drain and give them a quick rinse before using, and keep the jar refrigerated once opened.",
  "caramel-balsamic-glaze-modena":
    "This glaze blends Balsamic Vinegar of Modena with the smooth, buttery flavor of caramel for a drizzle that works for both sweet and savory dishes. Pour it over vanilla gelato, a slice of cheesecake, or pancakes on a lazy morning. On the savory side, it is wonderful with roasted pears and aged cheese, sweet potatoes, or a platter of roasted chicken thighs. Keep the bottle in the pantry and give it a gentle squeeze to drizzle.",
  "caramel-dessert-sauce-730621":
    "A smooth, buttery caramel sauce made in Italy, ready to pour over your favorite desserts. Drizzle it over gelato or vanilla ice cream, a slice of cheesecake, warm apple pie, or a stack of pancakes. Swirl a spoonful into coffee or hot chocolate, or use it to dip sliced apples and pears. Warm it gently for an even silkier pour.",
  "castelvetrano-olives-tray-730080":
    "Castelvetrano olives in a ready-to-serve tray. These bright green olives are known for their firm, meaty bite and mild, buttery, almost sweet flavor, which makes them a favorite even with people who are new to olives. Peel back the lid and serve them with cheese, crackers, and slices of fresh orange, or warm them briefly in olive oil with lemon zest and rosemary for an easy appetizer.",
  "cauliflower-gnocchi":
    "Soft Italian gnocchi made with cauliflower and potato, shelf-stable and ready in minutes. They cook just like classic gnocchi: drop them into boiling salted water and lift them out as soon as they float, or pan-fry them in olive oil until golden and crisp at the edges. Toss them with brown butter and sage, a fresh tomato sauce, or pesto, and finish with grated cheese.",
  "chili-pepper-grinder":
    "Dried chili peppers in a built-in grinder for freshly ground heat whenever you want it, made in Italy. Grinding just before use releases the chili's fruity, vibrant aroma and a warmth that lingers. Add a few turns to a pasta with garlic and olive oil, a slice of pizza, a pot of tomato soup, or a pan of roasted vegetables. Start light and build up to the heat you like.",
  "chili-pepper-paste-730495":
    "An Italian chili pepper paste in a compact 1.94 oz pack, bringing concentrated warmth and fruity chili flavor wherever you need it. Stir a little into tomato sauce for an arrabbiata, blend it into olive oil for a spicy drizzle over pizza, or mix it into a marinade for chicken or fish. It is also good in soups, stews, and dips. Start with a small amount and adjust to taste.",
  "chocolate-bar-with-almonds-730591":
    "A classic Italian chocolate bar studded with almonds, made in Italy. The smooth chocolate and crunchy, toasty almonds play off each other in every bite. Break off a square with your afternoon coffee, pack it for a road trip, or chop it roughly and fold it into cookie dough or a batch of brownies. It also makes a quick dessert board alongside dried apricots, fresh grapes, and a few pieces of biscotti.",
  "chocolate-bar-with-cacao-nibs-730592":
    "This Italian chocolate bar is dotted with crunchy cacao nibs, the roasted pieces of the cocoa bean itself. They add a pleasant crunch and a deep, slightly nutty cocoa flavor to the smooth chocolate. Enjoy a piece with coffee, crumble it over yogurt or a bowl of ice cream, or chop it into banana bread for little pockets of chocolate. Store it in a cool, dry spot.",
  "chocolate-dessert-sauce-730620":
    "A rich, glossy chocolate sauce made in Italy, the easy finishing touch for any dessert. Pour it over gelato, profiteroles, or a brownie sundae, drizzle it over strawberries and bananas, or stir it into warm milk for a quick hot chocolate. Warm it slightly for a smoother pour, and keep the bottle in the fridge once opened. It is also a quick way to dress up a plain sponge cake or a bowl of popcorn for movie night.",
  "chocolate-gianduiotti":
    "Gianduiotti are the boat-shaped chocolates of Turin, made from smooth chocolate blended with finely ground roasted hazelnuts. That blend, called gianduia, gives them a creamy, nutty sweetness that melts slowly. Each piece is individually wrapped in foil, so they are easy to share, pack in a lunch, or set out in a bowl for guests. Enjoy one with an espresso, or chop a few over vanilla ice cream for a quick Italian-style dessert.",
  "chocolate-truffle-dark":
    "Made in Lombardy in northern Italy, these truffles wrap a soft, silky ganache center in rich dark chocolate. The flavor is deep and gently bittersweet, with a smooth finish that lingers. Serve them with a strong espresso after dinner, set them on a dessert platter with dried figs and toasted almonds, or bring the box as a gift when you are invited for a meal. Keep them in a cool, dry place so the chocolate stays glossy.",
  "chocolate-truffle-hazelnut":
    "These truffles combine chocolate and roasted hazelnuts in one bite. Made in Lombardy, each truffle combines creamy milk chocolate with the warm, toasty flavor of hazelnuts and a soft center. Serve them with coffee or hot chocolate, add them to a holiday cookie tray, or wrap the box as a hostess gift. Store them somewhere cool and dry.",
  "chocolate-truffle-milk":
    "These milk chocolate truffles are made in Lombardy, in northern Italy, using classic European chocolate-making methods. Each one has a smooth, creamy milk chocolate shell and a soft center that melts slowly on the tongue. Set a few out with espresso after dinner, tuck them into a gift basket, or keep the box handy for a sweet moment in the afternoon. They pair nicely with fresh strawberries and a glass of sparkling grape juice. Store them in a cool, dry place away from heat.",
  "chocolate-truffle-pistachio":
    "These milk chocolate truffles are filled with the sweet, nutty flavor of pistachio, a favorite in Sicilian desserts. Made in Italy, they have a smooth shell and a soft, creamy center with a pale green pistachio note. Serve them after dinner with espresso, set them on a dessert board with fresh berries, or give the box as a thoughtful little gift. Keep them in a cool, dry spot.",
  "chopped-calabrian-chili-peppers":
    "Calabrian chili peppers from southern Italy, already chopped and packed in oil, so you can spoon in bold, tangy, spicy flavor in seconds. Stir a little into a tomato sauce for a quick arrabbiata, mix it into mayonnaise for a spicy sandwich spread, swirl it into hummus, or spoon it over pizza and roasted vegetables. Start with a small amount and add to taste. Keep the jar refrigerated once opened.",
  "classic-marinara-sauce":
    "Our classic marinara is made in Italy from ripe tomatoes with garlic and basil, simmered into a bright, simple sauce that lets the tomato shine. Heat it in a pan while the pasta cooks, then toss them together with a splash of the pasta water and a little olive oil. It is just as good layered into lasagna, spooned over eggplant parmigiana, or served warm as a dip for mozzarella sticks and garlic knots.",
  "classic-olive-oil-potato-chips":
    "Italian potato chips cooked in extra virgin olive oil, simply salted so the flavor of the potato and the oil come through. They fry up golden, crisp, and rich. Pour them into a bowl for an aperitivo with olives and a cold sparkling drink, serve them alongside a panini or a tuna sandwich, or crumble a handful over a salad for crunch.",
  "classic-potato-chips-730540":
    "Classic potato chips made in Italy, thin, golden, crisp, and simply salted. They are the everyday chip that goes with everything: a deli sandwich, a bowl of tomato soup, or a picnic spread. Pour them into a bowl next to olives and cheese for an easy aperitivo, or crush a handful over a casserole for a crunchy topping.",
  "classic-potato-chips-snack-bag":
    "Our classic olive oil potato chips in a single-serve 1.1 oz bag. They are golden, crisp, and simply salted, just the right portion for a lunchbox, a backpack, a desk drawer, or a road trip. Pair a bag with a sandwich and a sparkling drink for an easy lunch on the go. Keep a few bags in the pantry so there is always a crunchy, salty snack ready to grab on the way out the door.",
  "classico-margherita-pizza":
    "The classic Neapolitan pizza, made in Italy: San Marzano-style tomato sauce, creamy mozzarella, and fragrant basil on a crisp, golden crust. It is simple, honest, and always a favorite. Bake it straight from the freezer following the package directions until the cheese melts and bubbles. Tear a few fresh basil leaves over the top and add a drizzle of good olive oil just before slicing.",
  "coarse-mediterranean-sea-salt":
    "Large, crunchy sea salt crystals, made for a salt grinder, for salting pasta water, for brining, and for crusting a roast or a whole fish. Sprinkle a few crystals over sliced tomatoes or warm focaccia just before serving for a clean, satisfying crunch.",
  "cracked-marinated-olives":
    "These olives are gently cracked before marinating, an old Mediterranean technique that lets the herbs and olive oil soak right into the fruit. The result is a firm, juicy olive full of flavor in every bite. Serve them in a small bowl with a little of the marinade, alongside cheese, salami-style deli, and grissini. Add them to a warm potato salad, or spoon them over grilled fish with a squeeze of lemon. Note that they still have their pits.",
  "crushed-tomatoes-14oz":
    "Crushed tomatoes with no salt added, in a handy 14.1 oz size. They have a bright, rich tomato flavor and a rustic texture that is perfect for quick sauces. Warm them with garlic and olive oil for a fast pasta sauce for two, spread them on a homemade pizza, or stir them into soups, chili, and stews. Since there is no added salt, you can season exactly to your taste.",
  "crushed-tomatoes-24oz":
    "Italian tomatoes, coarsely crushed and packed in glass to keep their bright flavor. They are made for chunky sauces. Simmer them with garlic and olive oil for a quick sugo, build a hearty chili or a pot of minestrone, or cook eggs right in the sauce for shakshuka. They also make a great base for a baked pasta with plenty of cheese.",
  "dark-smooth-chocolate-bar-730590":
    "A dark chocolate bar made in Italy, with a deep cocoa flavor and a smooth melt. It is rich without being harsh, so it is easy to enjoy a square at a time. Pair it with espresso or a glass of sparkling grape juice, shave it over a bowl of berries and cream, or melt it down for a quick chocolate sauce to spoon over gelato. Store it somewhere cool and dry.",
  "diced-tomatoes-14oz":
    "Our diced Italian tomatoes in a smaller 14.1 oz size, just right for a weeknight dinner or a recipe that needs a measured amount. The even pieces hold their shape as they cook, so you get tender bites of tomato in every spoonful. Simmer them with olive oil, garlic, and oregano for a quick sauce, stir them into a pot of lentil or vegetable soup, or bake them over fish fillets with olives and capers.",
  "diced-tomatoes-24oz":
    "Ripe Italian tomatoes cut into even dice that hold their shape as they cook. They are perfect when you want pieces of tomato in the finished dish: chunky pasta sauces, vegetable soups, Mediterranean stews with chickpeas, or a quick bruschetta topping warmed with garlic and basil. Add them straight from the jar, juices and all, and let them simmer until the flavors come together.",
  "diet-cola":
    "All the refreshment of our Italian cola with zero sugar. It is made with natural flavors and sweetened without aspartame, and it has the same balanced, gently spiced cola taste, served in an elegant glass bottle. Keep a few in the fridge and pour it ice cold with a slice of lemon or lime. It goes well with pizza, a falafel plate, grilled burgers, or a big bowl of popcorn on movie night.",
  "elbows":
    "Classic elbow macaroni made in Italy from durum wheat semolina, cooked in 7 to 10 minutes. The short, curved tubes are made for creamy, cheesy sauces that tuck right inside. Use them for a bubbling baked mac and cheese, a cold pasta salad with vegetables and a tangy dressing, or a hearty minestrone. Kids love them with butter and a sprinkle of grated cheese.",
  "evoo-750ml":
    "Our Extra Virgin Olive Oil is cold-pressed from Italian olives, with a fruity aroma, golden-green color, and peppery finish. This is the bottle for finishing: drizzle it over a bowl of pasta, a ripe tomato salad, or warm beans, or pour a little into a dish with salt and pepper for dipping crusty bread. A spoonful over grilled fish or vegetables just before serving brings everything together. Store it away from heat and sunlight.",
  "evoo-black-truffle-250ml":
    "Our black truffle oil is made with Italian extra virgin olive oil, with truffle shavings in the bottle. A few drops bring the deep, earthy aroma of truffle to simple foods. Use it as a finishing oil, never for frying: drizzle it over fresh pasta with butter and parmesan, a creamy mushroom risotto, scrambled eggs, mashed potatoes, or a bowl of hot popcorn. A little goes a long way, so start with a light touch.",
  "evoo-garlic-250ml":
    "Cold-pressed Italian extra virgin olive oil infused with the warm, savory flavor of garlic, with no peeling or chopping needed. Drizzle it over toasted bread and top with tomatoes for an instant bruschetta, toss it with hot spaghetti and parsley for a quick aglio e olio, or brush it on vegetables before roasting. It is also delicious on popcorn, mashed potatoes, and grilled fish. Keep the bottle near the stove and away from direct sunlight.",
  "evoo-lemon-250ml":
    "This cold-pressed Italian extra virgin olive oil is infused with bright lemon flavor, fresh and zesty with a smooth finish. It is made for fish and seafood: drizzle it over grilled salmon or roasted branzino just before serving. Whisk it with a little salt for a quick salad dressing, toss it with steamed green beans or asparagus, or use it in place of regular oil in a lemon olive oil cake. Store it in a cool spot away from light.",
  "extra-light-olive-oil-1l":
    "Made in Italy from Italian olives, our Extra Light Olive Oil is refined for a clean, mild taste and a light bouquet that stays in the background. That makes it the everyday oil for frying, sautéing, roasting, and baking, anywhere you want olive oil without a strong olive flavor. Use it to fry crisp eggplant cutlets, roast a tray of potatoes, or bake a tender olive oil cake. Store the bottle away from heat and light, and keep it close to the stove.",
  "extra-light-olive-oil-2l":
    "Our Extra Light Olive Oil in a two-liter bottle for kitchens that cook every day. It is made in Italy and refined for a mild, neutral flavor and a higher smoke point, so it handles high-heat cooking with ease. Reach for it when you fry schnitzel or zucchini fritters, stir-fry vegetables, or bake muffins and cakes where you want a light, clean taste. Keep the bottle tightly closed in a cool, dark cupboard.",
  "extra-light-olive-oil-3l":
    "Our largest bottle of Extra Light Olive Oil, made in Italy for households that go through oil quickly. Its smooth, subtle flavor and light character make it a versatile workhorse: fry, sauté, roast, grill, and bake with it without overpowering the food. Use it for holiday latkes, crispy roasted chicken, or a big batch of fried peppers and onions. Decant a little into a smaller bottle for the counter and keep the rest in a cool, dark place.",
  "fettuccine":
    "Broad, flat ribbons of fettuccine made in Italy from durum wheat semolina and bronze cut, which gives each ribbon a slightly rough surface that holds on to sauce. Cook it in plenty of salted water for 9 to 12 minutes, until tender with a little bite. It is perfect for creamy sauces like Alfredo, for a slow-cooked Bolognese, or simply with butter, black pepper, and grated cheese.",
  "fettuccine-pasta-730321":
    "Italian fettuccine made from durum wheat, wide, flat ribbons that are made for rich sauces. Cook them in plenty of salted water until tender with a little bite. Toss them with a creamy Alfredo, a slow-cooked ragù, or simply butter, black pepper, and grated cheese. For an easy weeknight dinner, add sautéed mushrooms and a splash of cream.",
  "fine-mediterranean-sea-salt":
    "Fine sea salt milled to a free-flowing grain that dissolves quickly and seasons evenly. It is the everyday salt for the stove and the oven: season sauces and soups as they cook, mix it into bread and pizza dough, and use it in cakes and cookies. Keep the tube next to the stove and season a little at a time, tasting as you go.",
  "focaccia-bread-730010":
    "Italian focaccia, frozen to keep it fresh until you are ready to warm it. Heat it in the oven following the package directions until the outside is golden and the inside is soft and airy. Serve it warm with a dish of extra virgin olive oil and balsamic for dipping, split it for sandwiches with tuna or grilled vegetables, or set it alongside a bowl of soup or a big salad.",
  "forest-fruits-fruit-spread-preserves":
    "A spread of mixed forest berries with no high fructose corn syrup. The berries bring a deep color and a sweet-tart, layered flavor that is more complex than any single fruit. Spread it on toast or pancakes, swirl it into yogurt, or use it to fill a crostata or a batch of thumbprint cookies. It also pairs beautifully with soft cheeses and crackers on a cheese board.",
  "four-cheese-pizza":
    "A frozen pizza made in Italy, with a blend of four cheeses melted over tomato sauce on a golden, crisp crust. Each slice brings together creamy, tangy, and sharp cheese flavors. Bake it straight from the freezer following the package directions, until the cheese is bubbling and the edges are browned. Serve it with a simple arugula salad dressed with olive oil and lemon, and finish with a drizzle of chili oil if you like a little heat.",
  "fries-crinkle-cut":
    "Classic crinkle cut fries in a 24 oz bag, with wavy ridges that crisp up beautifully and hold on to salt and seasoning. Bake or air-fry them straight from frozen until golden, following the package directions. Serve them with burgers, hot dogs, or fish, with ketchup or a garlicky dipping sauce, and finish them hot with a sprinkle of sea salt flakes.",
  "fries-gondola":
    "Tuscanini Gondola Fries, a 24 oz bag of frozen fries ready to bake, air-fry, or fry to golden and crisp. They are an easy side for burgers, schnitzel, grilled chicken, or fish, and a fun snack on their own. Season them hot with sea salt, or try a pinch of truffle salt or a dusting of grated Parmesan and parsley. See the package for full preparation directions.",
  "fries-shoestring":
    "Thin, shoestring fries in a family-size 32 oz bag that cook up quickly and turn extra crisp. They are perfect next to a steak, a burger, or a crispy chicken sandwich. Bake, air-fry, or fry them from frozen following the package directions, then toss them hot with sea salt, a little chopped rosemary, or truffle salt for a restaurant-style finish.",
  "fries-straight-cut":
    "Classic straight cut fries in a family-size 32 oz bag, the everyday fry that goes with everything. Bake, air-fry, or fry them from frozen until golden and crisp, following the package directions. Serve them with burgers, schnitzel, or fish, and finish them hot with sea salt. For a treat, top them with grated Parmesan, garlic, and parsley. Kids and grown-ups alike will go back for seconds.",
  "frozen-cauliflower-gnocchi-730553":
    "Italian gnocchi made with cauliflower, frozen to keep their soft, tender texture. Cook them straight from frozen: pan-fry in olive oil until golden and lightly crisp, or boil until they float. They are lovely with pesto and cherry tomatoes, a simple marinara, or brown butter, garlic, and parmesan. Keep them in the freezer for an easy weeknight dinner.",
  "frozen-gluten-free-potato-gnocchi-730551":
    "Soft Italian potato gnocchi made gluten-free and frozen to keep their tender, fresh texture. Cook them straight from the freezer: boil until they float, or sauté in olive oil until golden on the outside. Serve them with tomato sauce and basil, pesto, or brown butter and sage, so the whole table can share a classic gnocchi dinner. Check the package for full ingredients and directions.",
  "frozen-potato-gnocchi-730550":
    "Soft, pillowy Italian potato gnocchi, frozen to lock in their fresh texture. Cook them straight from frozen: drop them into boiling salted water and lift them out as they float, or sauté them in a hot pan with olive oil until golden. Serve them with butter and sage, a simple tomato sauce, or pesto, and finish with grated cheese. Keep the bag in the freezer until you are ready to cook.",
  "frozen-potato-gnocchi-with-spinach-730552":
    "Soft Italian potato gnocchi with spinach worked right into the dough, which gives them a pretty green color and a gentle, fresh flavor. They go straight from the freezer to the pot: boil until they float, or sauté in butter or olive oil until lightly golden. Serve them with a creamy cheese sauce, a simple tomato sauce, or brown butter with sage and a shower of grated cheese.",
  "fusilli":
    "Bronze-cut fusilli made in Italy from durum wheat semolina. The tight corkscrew spirals trap sauce between every turn, so each bite carries plenty of flavor. Cook it for about 13 minutes in salted water. Serve it warm with pesto, a chunky vegetable sauce, or a creamy tomato sauce, or let it cool for a pasta salad with cherry tomatoes, olives, mozzarella, and basil.",
  "fusilli-pasta-730325":
    "Italian fusilli made from durum wheat, with spirals that catch sauce in every turn. It is a favorite for both warm dishes and cold salads. Toss it with pesto and cherry tomatoes, a chunky vegetable sauce, or a creamy tomato sauce. For a summer pasta salad, cool it after cooking and mix it with olives, mozzarella, roasted peppers, and a splash of olive oil and vinegar.",
  "garlic-paste-730496":
    "An Italian garlic paste made with olive oil and just three simple ingredients, in a ready-to-use squeeze tube. It delivers rich, savory garlic flavor without peeling, chopping, or garlicky fingers. Squeeze a little into a pan of olive oil to start a sauce, stir it into marinades and salad dressings, rub it on chicken or vegetables before roasting, or mix it with butter and parsley for quick garlic bread. Refrigerate after opening.",
  "garlic-pitted-olives-pouch":
    "Pitted Italian green olives with a bold garlic flavor, packed in single-serve pouches with no oil. They are savory and aromatic, with a firm, satisfying bite. Toss a pouch into a lunchbox or a travel bag, enjoy them with crackers and cheese at your desk, or scatter them over a salad or a bowl of pasta for a quick flavor boost. The sealed pouch keeps them fresh and ready whenever you are.",
  "gluten-free-potato-gnocchi":
    "Soft Italian potato gnocchi made with gluten-free flour, so everyone at the table can enjoy a classic gnocchi dinner. They are shelf-stable and ready in minutes: boil them until they float, then toss with your sauce. Try them with a bright tomato sauce, pesto, or brown butter and sage, or pan-fry them in olive oil until golden. Check the package for full ingredients and cooking directions.",
  "green-cerignola":
    "Cerignola olives are among the largest olives in the world, with a firm, crisp bite and a mild, smooth, slightly sweet flavor. Their size and bright green color make them the star of any antipasti board. Serve them in a small bowl next to sliced cheese, grissini, and roasted peppers, or marinate them with olive oil, lemon zest, garlic, and chili for a few hours before guests arrive. Keep the pits in mind when serving.",
  "green-cerignola-olives-tray-730083":
    "Big, bright green Cerignola olives in a ready-to-serve tray. Cerignolas are among the largest olives in the world, with a firm, crisp bite and a mild, gently sweet flavor that makes them the centerpiece of an antipasti spread. Open the tray and set them out next to cheese, grissini, and roasted peppers, with a small dish for the pits. They are perfect for a holiday table or an easy evening with friends.",
  "grilled-vegetable-pizza":
    "A frozen pizza made in Italy, topped with a colorful mix of grilled vegetables like peppers, zucchini, eggplant, and onions over mozzarella and tomato sauce. The vegetables bring a light smoky flavor to every slice. Bake it from frozen following the package directions until the crust is crisp. Serve it with a green salad, and add a drizzle of balsamic glaze over the top for a sweet, tangy finish.",
  "high-gluten-flour-5lb":
    "A high-gluten bread flour milled in Italy and pre-sifted, with extra gluten strength that builds a strong, elastic dough and a good rise. It is made for challah, bagels, rolls, rustic loaves, and chewy pizza crusts. Knead it well and give the dough time to rest, and you will see the difference in the stretch and the crumb. The 5 lb bag is sized for regular bakers.",
  "hot-sauce-potato-chips-snack-bag-730548":
    "Crisp potato chips with a hot sauce seasoning that brings tang and a pleasant, building heat. The single-serve 1.1 oz bag is ready for a lunchbox, a backpack, or a car ride. Pair them with a cold sparkling drink to balance the spice, or crumble a few over a taco salad. Keep a few bags handy for anyone at home who likes a little heat.",
  "italian-cola":
    "Our Italian cola is made with organic ingredients and natural flavors, with a balanced, less sugary sweetness and warm notes of spice. It comes in an elegant glass bottle that keeps the bubbles crisp and cold. Serve it chilled with a wedge of lemon for a classic Italian-café touch. It is a natural partner for pizza, a stacked deli sandwich, or a plate of burgers and fries, and it feels a little more special on the table than the usual can.",
  "italian-medley-grinder":
    "A blend of classic Italian herbs and spices in a built-in grinder, so the seasoning is freshly ground and fragrant every time. A few twists add instant Italian flavor without reaching for five different jars. Grind it over a bowl of pasta with olive oil, onto a pizza before baking, into a tomato sauce, or over roasted potatoes and chicken. It is also great mixed into olive oil as a dip for warm bread.",
  "italian-olives-trio-platter":
    "Three Italian olive varieties, each in its own compartment of a divided platter, so you can open, peel back the lid, and serve. It makes an instant, good-looking appetizer when guests drop by, with no bowls to wash. Set it out next to crackers, sliced cheese, and roasted peppers for an easy antipasti spread, or bring it along to a picnic or a holiday table. Let everyone discover their favorite of the three.",
  "kalamata-olives-14oz":
    "A larger jar of Kalamata olives for families who go through them fast. Kalamatas have a deep purple color, a smooth, meaty texture, and a rich, fruity, almost wine-like flavor. Keep the jar open in the fridge for snacking, set a bowl out with feta and warm pita, or simmer them into a chicken or fish dish with tomatoes, capers, and oregano. They are also the classic olive for a chopped Greek salad or a slow-roasted tray of vegetables. Mind the pits when serving.",
  "ketchup-potato-chips-730542":
    "Crisp potato chips made in Italy, with a sweet, tangy ketchup seasoning that tastes like fries and ketchup in a single crunch. Kids love them, and so do grown-ups. Serve them next to burgers or hot dogs at a barbecue, add them to a lunchbox, or bring the bag along for movie night. They are a guaranteed hit in a party bowl, so you may want to grab a second bag.",
  "kosher-salt-bulk":
    "A three-pound bag of coarse kosher salt. Its larger crystals are easy to pinch and scatter evenly, which is why cooks reach for it all day long. Use it to salt pasta water, season meat and vegetables before roasting, brine a chicken, or make a salt crust for whole fish. The bulk bag means you always have plenty on hand.",
  "large-black-truffle-sauce":
    "Our black summer truffle sauce in a large 17.6 oz jar for kitchens that use it often, from busy home cooks to caterers. Black truffles and mushrooms are blended with olive oil into a rich, earthy sauce. Toss it with pasta, drizzle it over pizza or fries, spread it on bruschetta, or spoon it alongside grilled meat and roasted vegetables. Keep the opened jar in the fridge.",
  "lemon-ginger-fruit-spread-preserves":
    "A fruit spread made from lemons and ginger, with 35% fruit and no high fructose corn syrup. It is bright, tangy, and gently spicy. Spread it on scones or buttered toast, spoon it over cheesecake or plain yogurt, or whisk a spoonful into a glaze for salmon or chicken. It is also lovely stirred into a cup of hot tea.",
  "lemon-juice-16oz":
    "Our lemon juice in a larger 16.9 oz bottle for kitchens that use lemon every day. It is not from concentrate, with no water added, so it has a bright, clean, tart flavor. Pour it into a pitcher of lemonade, whisk it into dressings and marinades, bake it into lemon bars and cakes, or squeeze it over a platter of roasted vegetables. Keep it in the fridge once opened.",
  "lemon-juice-6oz":
    "Not from concentrate and with no added water, this lemon juice brings bright, fresh citrus to the kitchen without slicing a single lemon. The lemon-shaped squeeze bottle makes it easy to add just a few drops or a generous squirt. Use it over grilled fish and chicken, in salad dressings, hummus, and marinades, in lemonade and iced tea, or in a lemon glaze for cake. Refrigerate after opening.",
  "lemon-sorbetto-730533":
    "A bright, refreshing lemon sorbetto made in Italy, smooth and icy-cold with the tart, sunny flavor of lemon. Serve a scoop between courses as a palate cleanser, after a rich dinner as a light dessert, or on a hot afternoon all on its own. For a sparkling treat, drop a scoop into a glass of sparkling lemonade or Moscato grape juice. Keep it frozen and let it soften for a minute before scooping.",
  "lemonade-730394":
    "A classic still lemonade made in Italy, in a generous 32 oz bottle for the whole family. It balances tart lemon with a gentle sweetness for a fresh, sunny flavor. Pour it over plenty of ice with lemon slices and a sprig of mint, or top it off with sparkling water for a fizzy version. It is a natural for summer barbecues, long family lunches, and picnics in the park. Shake well and keep it in the fridge once opened.",
  "lime-juice-730288":
    "Bottled in Italy, our lime juice has a bright, zesty, tangy flavor and comes in a lime-shaped squeeze bottle for easy, mess-free pouring. Skip the slicing and squeezing and add a splash wherever lime belongs: guacamole and salsa, fish tacos, grilled chicken marinades, a rice salad with herbs, or a pitcher of limeade with fresh mint. It is also great in baking, like a quick key lime-style pie. Refrigerate after opening.",
  "lime-juice-large-730289":
    "Our Italian lime juice in a larger 16.9 oz bottle, with the same bright, zesty flavor for cooking, baking, and drinks. It saves you from squeezing a bag of limes when a recipe calls for a lot of juice. Use it in a big bowl of guacamole, a batch of ceviche-style fish, a lime and herb marinade for grilling, or a pitcher of limeade for a summer gathering. Keep the bottle in the fridge once opened.",
  "mac-cheese-sauce-730225":
    "A creamy, cheesy sauce made in Italy, so mac and cheese is ready in the time it takes to boil the pasta. Toss it with hot elbows, shells, or cavatappi and serve as is, or spread it in a baking dish, top with breadcrumbs, and bake until golden and bubbling. It is also a handy sauce for steamed broccoli, baked potatoes, or a quick nacho-style snack. Warm it gently and stir well.",
  "mandarin-juice":
    "This Italian mandarin juice is sweet, fragrant, and gently tangy, with the soft, floral citrus flavor that sets mandarins apart from ordinary oranges. Serve it cold on its own, or use it as a mixer with sparkling water and a few ice cubes for a light afternoon drink. It is also a nice way to finish a sauce for roast chicken or duck, and a splash brightens up a fruit salad. Shake well and keep the bottle in the fridge once opened.",
  "minced-black-truffle":
    "Finely minced Italian black truffle in extra virgin olive oil, ready to spoon straight from the jar. It is an easy way to add truffle flavor to a dish. Fold it into softened butter for a truffle butter, stir it into mashed potatoes or a cream sauce, whisk it into a vinaigrette, or mix it into a burger or a mushroom filling. A small spoonful goes a long way. Refrigerate after opening.",
  "mini-focaccia-bread-730013":
    "Two individual focaccia breads made in Italy from double-risen, hand-stretched dough with extra virgin olive oil, frozen until you are ready to use them. Each bread is ready to top: spread on tomato sauce and mozzarella for a quick personal pizza, add pesto and cherry tomatoes, or keep it simple with a drizzle of olive oil and a pinch of sea salt. Bake following the package directions until golden. They are also the right size to split for sandwiches or to serve warm alongside soup or salad.",
  "mini-gnocchi":
    "Little Italian potato gnocchi, tender and bite-sized, ready in just a few minutes. Their small size makes them wonderfully versatile. Simmer them in a broth or minestrone for a hearty soup, toss them with butter and sage, or pan-fry them until golden and fold them into a salad with roasted vegetables. Kids love them with tomato sauce and a sprinkle of cheese.",
  "mini-margherita-calzones":
    "Bite-sized calzones made in Italy, with golden dough folded around melted mozzarella and tomato sauce. They are just right for appetizers, parties, lunchboxes, or an after-school snack. Bake them from frozen following the package directions until crisp and golden. Serve them warm with a small bowl of marinara for dipping and a sprinkle of grated cheese on top.",
  "mini-mushroom-pizza-calzones":
    "Little calzones made in Italy, filled with mushrooms, melted mozzarella, and tomato sauce inside a crisp, golden dough. They bring all the flavor of a mushroom pizza in a handheld bite. Bake them from frozen following the package directions and serve them warm as an appetizer, a party snack, or a quick lunch, with marinara for dipping. Keep a bag in the freezer for unexpected guests or a quick snack.",
  "moscato-grape-juice":
    "Made from Moscato grapes, this sparkling juice pours bright and lightly sweet, with a fine, lively fizz and the floral, fruity notes the grape is known for. It is completely non-alcoholic, so everyone at the table can raise a glass, and the tall blue bottle looks right at home on a holiday table. Serve it well chilled in flutes or wine glasses. It pairs beautifully with fruit platters, cheese, and light desserts, or try it over a few frozen grapes for an easy celebration drink.",
  "moscato-rose-juice":
    "The rosé sister of our sparkling Moscato, this juice is made from Italian grapes and pours a pretty blush pink with soft strawberry notes and a gentle, lively sparkle. It is non-alcoholic, so it works for every guest at the table, from the kids to the grandparents. Chill it well and serve it in flutes for birthdays, showers, and holiday dinners. It is lovely with strawberries and cream, a cheese plate, or a slice of almond cake, and makes an easy sparkling base for a fruit punch.",
  "mushroom-alfredo-sauce-730227":
    "A rich Alfredo-style sauce with the savory, earthy flavor of mushrooms, made for comforting pasta nights. Warm it gently and toss it with fettuccine or pappardelle, or spoon it over potato gnocchi and finish with black pepper and fresh thyme. It also makes a quick sauce for baked fish, a topping for roasted vegetables, or a creamy base for a mushroom lasagna. Heat over low and stir often.",
  "mushroom-pizza":
    "A frozen pizza made in Italy, topped generously with sliced mushrooms over melted mozzarella and tomato sauce on a golden crust. The earthy mushrooms and tangy sauce make it a satisfying vegetarian pizza. Bake it straight from the freezer following the package directions. For an extra touch, finish it with a few drops of truffle oil or a sprinkle of fresh thyme and black pepper.",
  "napoletana-pasta-sauce":
    "A Neapolitan-style pasta sauce made in Italy from ripe Italian tomatoes, slowly cooked with onion, garlic, and basil until rich, sweet, and silky. It is the kind of sauce that tastes like it simmered all afternoon. Warm it gently and toss it with spaghetti or rigatoni, finishing with a drizzle of olive oil and torn basil. It also makes a beautiful base for baked ziti, chicken parmigiana, or eggs poached right in the sauce.",
  "oregano-parchment-crackers-730331":
    "Paper-thin Italian parchment crackers seasoned with oregano, crisp and light with a warm, Mediterranean herb flavor. Serve them with hummus, a sun-dried tomato pesto, or a creamy cheese spread, or set them out on an antipasti board with olives and roasted peppers. They are also a crunchy side for a bowl of minestrone. Break them into pieces and scatter them over a salad for a crunchy finish.",
  "oregano-parchment-crackers-small-730335":
    "These paper-thin parchment crackers are made with olive oil and seasoned with oregano. They are delicate, crisp, and full of Mediterranean herb flavor. Break them over a salad, serve them with cheese and olives, or pair them with hummus or a sun-dried tomato spread. The 2.64 oz pack is just right for snacking or a small antipasti plate.",
  "organic-apple-cider-vinegar":
    "Our organic apple cider vinegar is unfiltered and unpasteurized, with the cloudy \"mother\" left in, which gives it a fuller, fruity apple tang. Shake it up with olive oil, honey, and mustard for a bright salad dressing, add a splash to a marinade for chicken, or use it for quick pickled red onions and cucumbers. A little in a pot of lentil soup or a barbecue sauce brightens the whole dish.",
  "organic-tomato-paste-tube":
    "A double-concentrated tomato paste made in Italy from organic Italian tomatoes, in a handy squeezable tube. A small spoonful goes a long way: cook it briefly in olive oil to deepen its flavor, then build a ragù, a vegetable soup, or a pot of beans around it. It also gives a quick boost to gravies, marinades, and shakshuka. The tube keeps the rest fresh in the fridge for next time.",
  "original-parchment-crackers-730330":
    "Paper-thin Italian parchment crackers, crisp and delicate, with a light, clean flavor that lets your toppings shine. Break them into shards and serve them on a cheese board, alongside olives, dips, and spreads, or with a bowl of soup. They are also lovely on their own with a drizzle of good olive oil and a pinch of sea salt.",
  "original-parchment-crackers-small-730334":
    "Our paper-thin Italian parchment crackers in a smaller 2.64 oz pack, just right for a lunchbox, a picnic, or a small cheese plate. They are delicate, shatteringly crisp, and lightly flavored so they pair with almost anything. Top them with cheese, tuna, or a spoonful of pesto, or enjoy them on their own as a light, crunchy snack.",
  "original-pitted-olives-pouch":
    "Pitted green olives packed in single-serve 1.06 oz pouches with no oil, so there is no mess and nothing to drain. They are mild and buttery, with the firm, meaty bite Castelvetranos are known for. Tuck a pouch into a lunchbox, a backpack, or a carry-on, or tear one open over a salad for an instant topper. Each pouch is sealed, so they stay fresh until you are ready.",
  "oven-ready-lasagna":
    "Flat, oven-ready lasagna sheets made in Italy from durum wheat semolina. No boiling needed: the sheets soak up moisture from the sauce as they bake, turning tender and holding their layers. Build your lasagna straight in the pan with tomato or meat sauce, ricotta, mozzarella, and a generous dusting of grated cheese, or layer in roasted vegetables and béchamel. Make sure every sheet is covered with sauce, then bake until golden and bubbling.",
  "panini-bread-730012":
    "Italian panini bread, frozen to keep it fresh, ready to warm up and fill. Heat it following the package directions, split it, and build your favorite sandwich: fresh mozzarella with tomato and basil, tuna with arugula and lemon, or grilled vegetables with pesto. Press it in a panini grill or a hot pan for a crisp, golden crust and a melty center.",
  "parmesan-cheese-wedge-5oz":
    "A wedge of Italian Parmesan, aged for a deep, nutty flavor and a crumbly, crystalline texture. Grate it fresh over pasta, risotto, and soup, shave thin curls over a salad of arugula and pears, or break off small chunks to serve with honey, walnuts, and a drizzle of balsamic. Save the rind and drop it into a pot of minestrone or tomato sauce for extra flavor. Wrap it well and keep it in the fridge.",
  "parmesan-cheese-wedge-8oz":
    "A larger 8.8 oz wedge of Italian Parmesan for families who grate it over everything. Aged for a rich, nutty flavor and a crumbly, crystalline texture, it is the finishing touch for pasta, risotto, and soups. Shave it over a salad of arugula and cherry tomatoes, bake it into crisp frico wafers, or serve small chunks with sliced pears, figs, and a drizzle of balsamic glaze. Wrap it well and keep it refrigerated.",
  "peeled-tomatoes":
    "Whole peeled Italian tomatoes, vine-ripened in rich volcanic soil and packed at peak flavor. They are the classic start to a homemade sauce: crush them by hand into a pan of warm olive oil and garlic, add a few basil leaves, and simmer until thick and sweet. Blend them smooth for a silky sauce or soup, or roast them with onions for a deeper flavor. A pantry staple for any Italian kitchen.",
  "penne":
    "Bronze-cut penne made in Italy from durum wheat semolina, with ridged tubes and angled ends that catch sauce inside and out. Cook it in well-salted boiling water for 11 to 14 minutes. Penne is a natural for a spicy arrabbiata, a creamy vodka sauce, or a baked pasta with tomato sauce and melted mozzarella. It also holds up well in a pasta salad with vegetables and olives.",
  "penne-pasta-730322":
    "Classic penne made in Italy from durum wheat, with angled ends and hollow tubes that hold sauce inside and out. It is one of the most versatile shapes in the pantry. Cook it in plenty of salted water until al dente, then toss it with a spicy arrabbiata, a creamy vodka sauce, or a simple marinara. Penne also bakes beautifully with tomato sauce and melted mozzarella.",
  "peppercorn-medley-grinder":
    "A blend of four peppercorn varieties in an easy-grip glass grinder, with no fillers. Together they bring layered flavor: warm heat from the black, gentle floral and fruity notes from the others. Grind it over grilled fish, roasted chicken, buttered pasta, or a salad of greens and pears, and use it to finish soups and creamy sauces. The colorful peppercorns look pretty on the table, too.",
  "personal-pie-thin-crust-pizza":
    "A thin-crust pizza sized just for one, with tomato sauce and melted mozzarella on an ultra-thin, crispy base. It is a quick lunch, a late-night snack, or an easy dinner when everyone wants their own. Bake it straight from the freezer following the package directions. Dress it up with a few olives, a sprinkle of chili flakes, or fresh basil.",
  "pitted-bella-italia-mix":
    "A colorful mix of Italian olive varieties in one jar, with greens and darks side by side, all pitted and ready to eat. Each olive brings its own character, from mild and buttery to rich and fruity, so every handful is a little different. Pour them into a bowl for an aperitivo with crackers and cheese, scatter them over a homemade pizza, or toss them into a pasta salad with cherry tomatoes, basil, and a splash of olive oil.",
  "pitted-bella-italia-olive-mix-tray-730082":
    "Our Bella Italia mix of Italian olives, pitted and packed in a ready-to-serve tray. The colorful medley brings together different varieties with flavors ranging from mild and buttery to rich and fruity. Peel back the lid and set it out with cheese, crackers, and grissini for an easy aperitivo, or spoon the olives over a pizza, a pasta salad, or roasted vegetables. It is a simple way to bring a little Italian table to any gathering.",
  "pitted-green-castelvetrano":
    "Castelvetrano olives come from western Sicily and are known for their bright green color, firm, meaty bite, and mild, buttery, almost sweet flavor, with none of the sharp saltiness of many olives. Ours are pitted, so they are ready to snack on straight from the jar. Set them out with cheese and crackers, toss them into a citrus and fennel salad, or warm them gently in olive oil with orange peel and herbs for an easy appetizer.",
  "pitted-green-olives-730376":
    "Classic pitted green olives in a handy 4.9 oz pack, firm and briny with a clean, savory flavor. With the pits already out, they are ready for snacking, cooking, or a quick appetizer. Set them out with crackers and cheese, slice them over pizza, fold them into a tuna or chicken salad, or add them to a tray of roasted vegetables in the last few minutes. A simple pantry favorite.",
  "pitted-green-olives-with-garlic-730377":
    "Pitted green olives seasoned with garlic, in a handy 4.9 oz pack. They are firm and briny, with a savory, aromatic garlic flavor that makes them easy to keep reaching for. Snack on them straight from the pack, set them out with crackers and cheese, or toss a handful into a pasta with cherry tomatoes and parsley. They also add a bold note to a chopped salad or a homemade pizza.",
  "pitted-green-olives-with-lemon-730378":
    "Pitted green olives with a fresh, zesty lemon flavor, in a convenient 4.9 oz pack. The bright citrus note lifts the olive's natural brininess and keeps every bite refreshing. Serve them with a cheese plate and sliced fennel, scatter them over grilled fish or a green salad, or chop them into a couscous or rice salad with herbs. They are a light, lively snack any time of day.",
  "pitted-kalamata":
    "Kalamata olives are known for their deep purple color and rich, almost wine-like flavor, and their flesh is smooth and meaty. We pit them for you, so they go straight from the jar to the cutting board or the bowl. Toss a handful into a Greek salad with cucumber, tomato, and red onion, fold them into a warm pasta with cherry tomatoes and olive oil, or chop them fine for a quick tapenade to spread on toasted bread. They also earn a spot on any antipasti board next to cheese and crackers.",
  "pitted-kalamata-olives-pouch-730196":
    "Rich, fruity Kalamata olives, pitted and portioned into a single-serve 1.06 oz pouch. Their deep purple color and smooth, meaty texture make them a satisfying savory snack anywhere: at school, at work, or on a long drive. Open one over a Greek salad, a bowl of hummus, or a wrap with feta and cucumber for a quick upgrade. No jar to open and no pits to worry about.",
  "pitted-kalamata-olives-tray-730081":
    "Pitted Kalamata olives in a ready-to-serve tray. Kalamatas have a deep purple color, a smooth, meaty texture, and a rich, fruity flavor with a hint of wine. With the pits already out, they are easy to snack on or to cook with. Peel back the lid and serve them with feta, cucumbers, and warm pita, or chop them into a quick tapenade, a Greek salad, or a tray of roasted vegetables.",
  "pitted-olive-trio-trays-730084":
    "A trio of pitted Italian olives in a ready-to-serve tray, with three varieties side by side so everyone can find a favorite. With the pits already out, they are easy for guests and kids to enjoy. Open the tray and set it on a cheese board, take it along to a picnic or a potluck, or use the olives in a quick pasta with cherry tomatoes, garlic, and olive oil. Antipasti, ready in seconds.",
  "pitted-olives-crushed-garlic":
    "Pitted Italian olives marinated with crushed garlic for a bold, savory, aromatic flavor. They are ready to serve straight from the jar, no extra seasoning needed. Set them out with crusty bread and a drizzle of olive oil, chop them into a quick tapenade, or toss them with spaghetti, cherry tomatoes, and parsley for a fast weeknight pasta. They are also delicious scattered over a sheet-pan of roasted vegetables or a homemade pizza.",
  "pizza-crust-730011":
    "A ready-made Italian pizza crust, frozen and waiting for your favorite toppings, so homemade pizza night takes minutes instead of hours. Spread it with pizza sauce, add mozzarella and whatever the family loves, from mushrooms and olives to peppers and onions, and bake following the package directions until the cheese bubbles and the edges turn golden. Finish with fresh basil and a drizzle of olive oil.",
  "pomegranate-juice":
    "Our pomegranate juice has a deep red color and a bold sweet-tart flavor. Pour it over ice on its own, or cut it with sparkling water for a lighter drink. It blends nicely into smoothies with banana and berries, and it makes a quick glaze when simmered down with a little honey to brush over roast chicken or drizzle over vanilla ice cream. For holidays, mix it with sparkling grape juice for a festive red punch. Shake well before pouring.",
  "potato-gnocchi":
    "Classic Italian potato gnocchi with a soft, pillowy texture, shelf-stable and ready in minutes. Drop them into boiling salted water and scoop them out as they float to the top. Serve them with a simple tomato and basil sauce, a creamy gorgonzola-style cheese sauce, or melted butter and sage. For a crisp finish, pan-fry the boiled gnocchi in olive oil until golden.",
  "raspberry-balsamic-glaze-modena":
    "Balsamic Vinegar of Modena slowly reduced and blended with the bright, tangy sweetness of raspberries into a thick, jewel-red glaze. Drizzle it over a salad of spinach, walnuts, and goat cheese, spoon it over fresh berries and whipped cream, or use it to finish a cheese board with crackers and sliced pears. It is also lovely on grilled chicken, roasted beets, and a scoop of vanilla gelato. The squeeze bottle makes it easy to plate beautifully.",
  "raspberry-dessert-sauce-730622":
    "A bright, fruity raspberry sauce made in Italy, with a sweet-tart berry flavor and a beautiful deep red color. Drizzle it over vanilla gelato or panna cotta, a slice of cheesecake or chocolate cake, or a bowl of fresh berries and cream. It also makes pancakes, waffles, and yogurt feel like a treat. Shake well before using. Drizzle a little over a chocolate dessert for a lovely color contrast.",
  "raspberry-fruit-spread-preserves":
    "A tangy raspberry spread with no high fructose corn syrup. Its jewel-red color and bold berry flavor make it as pretty as it is tasty. Spread it on toast or scones, layer it into a Linzer cookie or a chocolate cake, or spoon it over cheesecake. A spoonful whisked with balsamic vinegar and olive oil makes a lovely dressing for a spinach salad.",
  "red-cooking-wine":
    "Our red cooking wine is made in Italy from red and white grapes chosen to bring depth and aroma to savory dishes. Use it to deglaze the pan after searing meat, lifting all the browned bits into a sauce. Add a generous splash to a slow-simmered ragù, a pot of beef stew, or braised short ribs, and let it reduce so the flavor turns rich and rounded. It also works well in marinades and mushroom sauces.",
  "red-wine-vinegar":
    "Made in Italy from red wine, this vinegar has a deep ruby color and a bold, fruity tang. It is the backbone of a classic Italian vinaigrette with olive oil, oregano, salt, and pepper. Splash it into a tomato sauce or a pan of sautéed peppers, use it in marinades for chicken or beef, or sprinkle it over a chopped salad of cucumbers, tomatoes, and red onion. It is a pantry staple you will reach for again and again.",
  "reserve-bbq-ground-beef-pizza":
    "A Reserve pizza topped with seasoned ground beef and a tangy, smoky barbecue sauce. It is a bold, satisfying pie that brings Italian pizza-making together with barbecue flavor. Bake it from frozen following the package directions until the crust is crisp. Top it with thinly sliced red onion or pickled jalapeños for extra punch, and serve it with a crunchy coleslaw.",
  "reserve-margherita-pizza":
    "Our Reserve Margherita is made in Italy, topped with San Marzano-style tomato sauce and mozzarella. The crust bakes up airy and crisp. Bake it from frozen following the package directions until the cheese bubbles and the edges brown. Finish with fresh basil leaves and a thin drizzle of extra virgin olive oil.",
  "reserve-supermargherita-pizza":
    "The Reserve Supermargherita takes our margherita further, with extra mozzarella, cherry tomatoes, and basil over tomato sauce. It is generous, juicy, and full of fresh flavor. Bake it from frozen following the package directions until the crust is golden and the cherry tomatoes just blister. Add a little sea salt and a drizzle of olive oil before serving.",
  "rigatoni":
    "Large, ridged rigatoni made in Italy from durum wheat semolina. The wide tubes are made for hearty sauces: chunky tomato ragù, meat sauce, or roasted vegetables all find their way inside. Cook it in plenty of salted water for 12 to 15 minutes, until al dente. Try it with a slow-simmered sauce and grated cheese, or bake it with ricotta and mozzarella for a crowd-pleasing dinner.",
  "rippled-olive-oil-potato-chips":
    "Thick, rippled potato chips cooked in Italian extra virgin olive oil. The deep ridges give every chip an extra-hearty crunch and hold onto the seasoning. They are made for dipping: serve them with a creamy onion dip, a garlicky yogurt dip, or hummus, or pile them next to a burger or a deli sandwich. They also travel well in a picnic basket or a lunchbox, holding their crunch until you are ready to open the bag.",
  "rippled-potato-chips-730541":
    "Thick, rippled potato chips made in Italy, with deep ridges for an extra-satisfying crunch. They are sturdy enough to scoop up thick dips, so set them out with a creamy dip, salsa, or hummus. They are also a natural side for burgers, schnitzel sandwiches, and anything off the grill. Share the 4.6 oz bag, or not. Crumble a few over a tuna casserole for a crunchy topping.",
  "rippled-potato-chips-snack-bag":
    "Our extra-crunchy rippled olive oil potato chips in a grab-and-go 1.1 oz bag. The deep ridges deliver a satisfying crunch in every bite. Tuck a bag into a lunchbox or a picnic basket, or keep a few on hand for after school, a long drive, or an afternoon snack with a cold drink. They are sturdy enough for a quick dip in hummus, too.",
  "roasted-chestnuts":
    "Chestnuts, roasted, peeled, and ready to eat straight from the pouch. They are tender, creamy, and naturally sweet, with no shells to crack and no oven needed. Enjoy them as a snack on a cool afternoon, warm them briefly in a pan with butter and herbs as a side dish, or chop them into stuffing, a winter salad, a risotto, or a chocolate dessert.",
  "roasted-chestnuts-salt-black-pepper":
    "Our roasted Italian chestnuts, peeled and seasoned with sea salt and cracked black pepper. The savory seasoning plays off the chestnut's natural sweetness and creamy texture. Eat them straight from the pouch as a snack, set them out with cheese and dried fruit, or toss them warm over roasted Brussels sprouts or a green salad for a cozy, wintery touch.",
  "rosemary-olive-oil-potato-chips":
    "Italian potato chips cooked in extra virgin olive oil and seasoned with fragrant rosemary. Each crisp, golden chip carries a warm, herby aroma that feels straight out of a Tuscan kitchen. Serve them with a cheese board, alongside grilled chicken or a steak sandwich, or simply with a bowl of olives and a chilled sparkling lemonade. Pour them into a bowl and they will not last long.",
  "rosemary-parchment-crackers-730332":
    "Paper-thin Italian parchment crackers seasoned with fragrant rosemary. They are light, shatteringly crisp, and full of herby aroma. Serve them with soft cheeses, a tapenade, or a bowl of olives for an aperitivo, or alongside a tomato soup or a big green salad. They look beautiful standing in a glass on the table. A drizzle of olive oil and a pinch of sea salt is all they need.",
  "rosemary-parchment-crackers-small-730336":
    "Our rosemary parchment crackers in a smaller 2.64 oz pack. Paper-thin and crisp, they carry the warm, piney aroma of rosemary in every bite. Pack them for lunch with a wedge of cheese, set them out with olives for guests, or serve them alongside a bowl of soup. A light, elegant snack any time of day. They also make a crunchy topping crumbled over soup.",
  "salt-vinegar-potato-chips-730544":
    "Crisp potato chips made in Italy, with a bold salt and vinegar seasoning that is tangy, sharp, and impossible to stop eating. They are perfect with a fish sandwich, alongside fried fish and a lemon wedge, or on their own with a cold drink. Pack the 4.6 oz bag for a picnic or a game night. They are a great match for a tuna sandwich, too.",
  "sea-salt-flakes":
    "Pyramid-shaped sea salt flakes, made for finishing. They add a light crunch and a clean, bright saltiness without overwhelming the food. Crumble a pinch between your fingers over a steak or grilled fish, a ripe tomato salad, roasted vegetables, or a fried egg. They are also wonderful on chocolate chip cookies, caramel, and brownies right out of the oven.",
  "sicilian-extra-virgin-olive-oil-730406":
    "A single-origin extra virgin olive oil harvested and bottled in Sicily under P.G.I. standards, which trace the oil back to Sicilian groves. It is cold-extracted for a fruity, fresh flavor with the gentle green, peppery notes Sicilian olives are known for. Use it raw to get the most from it: over a caponata, a plate of sliced tomatoes and oregano, grilled vegetables, or a slice of warm bread with a pinch of sea salt. Store it away from light and heat.",
  "sliced-black-truffle":
    "Thin slices of Italian black truffle preserved in extra virgin olive oil, ready to lay over a finished dish. They bring a beautiful look and a deep, earthy aroma to the plate. Arrange a few slices over fresh pasta with butter and parmesan, a creamy risotto, a carpaccio, or soft scrambled eggs, and drizzle a little of the truffle-scented oil from the jar over the top. Refrigerate after opening.",
  "smoked-sea-salt-flakes":
    "Sea salt flakes, smoked for a deep, woodsy aroma and a crisp, flaky crunch. A pinch brings the flavor of the grill to food cooked indoors. Sprinkle it over grilled or roasted vegetables, salmon, potatoes, avocado toast, or scrambled eggs, and try it on caramel, chocolate, or roasted nuts for a sweet-smoky finish. Use it at the end of cooking so the flakes stay crunchy.",
  "solid-light-tuna-in-olive-oil-six-pack-730428":
    "A six-pack of our solid light tuna in olive oil, so the pantry is always ready for a quick meal. The tuna is tender and moist, with a rich, smooth flavor from the olive oil. Use it in pasta with lemon and capers, in a niçoise-style salad, in tuna melts, or flaked over a bowl of greens and beans. A handy stock-up for busy weeks.",
  "solid-light-tuna-in-water-three-pack-730424":
    "Three small cans of solid light tuna in water, each a handy single portion. The tuna has a clean, delicate flavor and firm pieces that take well to any dressing. Drain it and mix it with mayonnaise and celery, or dress it Italian-style with olive oil, lemon, and herbs. It is perfect for packed lunches, wraps, salads, and quick sandwiches.",
  "solid-light-tuna-olive-oil-chili-peppers-can":
    "Solid light yellowfin tuna packed in olive oil with Calabrian chili peppers for a gentle, warming heat. The spice brings out the tuna's rich flavor without overpowering it. Toss it with hot spaghetti, garlic, and parsley for a quick spicy pasta, pile it onto crusty bread with arugula, or mix it into a bean and red onion salad. Use the spicy oil in the can to dress the dish.",
  "solid-light-tuna-olive-oil-chili-peppers-three-pack":
    "Three small cans of solid light yellowfin tuna, packed in olive oil with Calabrian chili peppers. Each 2.82 oz can is a perfect single portion with a gentle, warming kick. Toss one with hot pasta and parsley, spoon it over a bowl of rice or a green salad, or pile it on crackers for a spicy snack. Drizzle the chili oil from the can over the top.",
  "solid-light-tuna-olive-oil-small-jar":
    "Solid light tuna packed in olive oil in a small glass jar, so you can see the firm, tender pieces before you open it. The olive oil keeps the tuna moist and adds a rich, smooth flavor. Flake it over a salad of greens, tomatoes, olives, and boiled potatoes, toss it with pasta, lemon, capers, and parsley, or set it on an antipasto platter with roasted peppers and crusty bread.",
  "solid-light-tuna-olive-oil-three-pack":
    "Three small 2.82 oz cans of our solid light tuna in olive oil, each one just right for a single meal. The tuna is tender and rich, and the olive oil keeps it moist and flavorful. Open a can for a quick lunch over greens, mix one into a pasta with tomatoes and olives, or pack one with crackers for an easy work lunch. Keep a few packs in the pantry for busy days.",
  "spaghetti":
    "Our spaghetti is made from durum wheat semolina and pushed through bronze dies, which leave a slightly rough, matte surface on every strand. That texture is what lets a sauce cling instead of sliding off, and slow drying keeps the bite firm. Cook it in plenty of well-salted water for 9 to 12 minutes, tasting near the end so you can pull it al dente. Save a cup of the cooking water before you drain. For a classic Roman plate, toss it with garlic, good olive oil, and a pinch of chili, or keep it simple with a fresh tomato and basil sauce.",
  "spaghetti-pasta-730320":
    "Classic Italian spaghetti made from durum wheat, the long, thin strand. Cook it in a big pot of well-salted boiling water and pull it out just al dente. Toss it with garlic, olive oil, and chili for a quick aglio e olio, a fresh tomato and basil sauce, or a hearty meatball marinara. Save a cup of pasta water to bring the sauce together.",
  "sparkling-apple-cider":
    "Made in Italy from Italian apples, this sparkling cider has a crisp, naturally sweet apple flavor and a festive fizz. It is non-alcoholic, so it is the bottle everyone can share at a holiday meal, a birthday, or a Friday night dinner. Serve it well chilled in flutes or wine glasses. It goes beautifully with roast chicken, a cheese board with sharp cheddar, or an apple tart, and a splash of it with cranberry juice makes a quick celebration punch.",
  "sparkling-bianco-grape-juice":
    "This sparkling juice is pressed from Italian white grapes and has a light, fruity taste with fine, lively bubbles. It is non-alcoholic, and the elegant 750 ml bottle looks right at home on a festive table. Chill it well before opening and pour it into flutes for a toast. It pairs well with fish, pasta in a light cream sauce, fresh fruit, and mild cheeses, and it is a welcome bottle to bring along when you are invited for a holiday meal.",
  "sparkling-blood-orange":
    "Blood oranges give this organic sparkling drink its ruby color and its sweet-tart, slightly berry-like citrus flavor. It is made with blood orange juice and no food coloring. Pour it ice cold into a glass with a slice of orange, or keep a few bottles in the fridge for an easy afternoon treat. It brightens up a pizza night, a grilled chicken dinner, or a simple antipasti spread with olives and crackers.",
  "sparkling-blood-orange-aranciata-730386":
    "Aranciata is Italy's classic sparkling orange drink, and ours is made with organic blood oranges. The fruit gives it a ruby color and a bright, sweet-tart flavor with a hint of berry, carried on crisp bubbles in a single-serve glass bottle. Serve it ice cold, on its own or over ice with a twist of orange peel. It is perfect with a slice of pizza, a panini at lunch, or an afternoon plate of biscotti.",
  "sparkling-blood-orange-aranciata-large-730387":
    "Aranciata is the classic Italian sparkling orange drink, and ours is made with organic blood oranges for a deep ruby color and a sweet-tart, slightly berry-like flavor. This large 25.3 oz glass bottle is made for sharing. Chill it well and pour it over ice with a twist of orange peel. It is the perfect bottle for a pizza night or a summer lunch outdoors, and it pairs beautifully with grilled chicken, focaccia, and a big green salad.",
  "sparkling-lemonade":
    "A bright, fizzy lemon drink made in Italy with lemons and organic ingredients. It is lightly sweetened, so the zesty, sunny flavor of the lemon comes through first, with crisp bubbles behind it. The single-serve glass bottle is just the right size for lunch, a picnic, or a long afternoon on the porch. Serve it ice cold, straight from the bottle or poured over ice with a sprig of fresh mint. It is especially good with grilled fish, a summer salad, or a plate of fried zucchini.",
  "sparkling-lemonade-730384":
    "A crisp sparkling lemonade made in Italy, with a lively fizz and a fresh, zesty lemon flavor that is lightly sweet rather than sugary. The single-serve 9.3 oz bottle is easy to pack for lunch, a picnic, or a day at the beach. Serve it ice cold, straight from the bottle or poured over ice with a slice of lemon. It is a refreshing partner for fried foods, grilled fish, and summer pasta salads.",
  "sparkling-lemonade-large-730385":
    "Our sparkling lemonade in the large, shareable 25.3 oz bottle. It is made in Italy, lightly sweetened, and full of zesty lemon flavor with crisp, fine bubbles. Set it on the table for a family lunch or a summer barbecue and pour it ice cold over plenty of ice, with lemon slices and a few mint leaves for color. It is especially refreshing alongside grilled fish, chicken skewers, and big summer salads.",
  "sparkling-malvasia-grape-juice-730472":
    "Malvasia is one of Italy's most aromatic white grapes, and this juice carries its fragrant, honeyed fruit notes with a gentle, bright sparkle. It is alcohol-free and comes in a Champagne-style bottle. Serve it well chilled in flutes for a toast, a holiday meal, or a quiet dinner at home. It pairs beautifully with soft cheeses, fresh peaches or melon, and light almond desserts.",
  "sparkling-rosato-grape-juice":
    "A rosy pink sparkling juice made in Italy from red and white grapes, with fruity notes of berries and stone fruit and a soft, refreshing fizz. It is non-alcoholic, so the whole table can share a toast. Serve it well chilled in flutes, or pour it over ice with a few raspberries for a pretty summer drink. It is a natural fit for a brunch spread, a fruit and cheese platter, or a dessert of berries and whipped cream.",
  "spelt-white-flour-5lb":
    "White spelt flour milled in Italy from spelt, an ancient grain, and pre-sifted for convenient baking. It has a mild, slightly nutty and sweet flavor and bakes into soft, tender breads. Use it for challah, sourdough, rolls, cookies, and cakes, either on its own or mixed with regular flour. Spelt dough is a little more delicate, so knead gently and avoid overworking it.",
  "spicy-pimiento-stuffed-olives":
    "Plump Italian olives stuffed with spicy pimiento peppers, with a pleasant kick of heat balanced by the olive's natural, briny flavor. They are a bold upgrade on the classic stuffed olive. Serve them on an appetizer board with cheese and crackers, slice them over pizza or into a chopped salad, or add them to a sandwich for a little fire. They also make a lively garnish for a Bloody Mary-style tomato juice.",
  "spicy-pitted-olives-pouch":
    "Pitted Italian green olives seasoned with a spicy blend and packed in single-serve pouches with no oil. They are firm and flavorful, with a kick of heat that builds as you go. Keep a few pouches in your bag, desk drawer, or glove box for a savory snack on the move, or open one over a salad, a grain bowl, or a slice of pizza for an instant spicy topping. No jar, no brine, no mess.",
  "strawberry-fruit-spread-preserves":
    "A strawberry spread made with 50% fruit and no high fructose corn syrup. Spread it on warm toast or a buttery croissant, swirl it into yogurt or oatmeal, or sandwich it between layers of a sponge cake with whipped cream. It is also lovely spooned over vanilla ice cream or a slice of cheesecake, and a natural partner for peanut butter in a lunchbox sandwich.",
  "sun-dried-tomato-pesto":
    "A rustic red pesto made with sun-dried tomatoes for a rich, tangy-sweet, deeply savory flavor. It is a bold twist on classic green pesto. Stir it into hot pasta, spread it on crostini or a wrap, use it as a pizza base, or mix a spoonful into cream cheese for a quick dip. It is also delicious spread over chicken or fish before baking. Refrigerate after opening.",
  "sun-dried-tomatoes":
    "Our sun-dried tomatoes are packed in olive oil, cut into thin julienne strips. Drying concentrates their sweetness and savory depth, and the oil keeps them soft and ready to use. Toss them into pasta with garlic and basil, layer them into a sandwich with fresh mozzarella, chop them into a grain salad, or scatter them over focaccia before baking. Save the flavorful oil for dressings.",
  "sweet-sicilian-castelvetrano":
    "A larger jar of Sicilian Castelvetrano olives, gently marinated to bring out their natural buttery sweetness. They are bright green, firm, and mild, with a gentle, fruity flavor that wins over people who think they do not like olives. Keep a jar open for snacking, set them out with a cheese board and focaccia, or chop them into a tuna or chicken salad. They also add a lovely sweet-salty note to a pan of roasted chicken.",
  "tomato-juice":
    "Made in Italy from Italian tomatoes and not from concentrate, this tomato juice has a smooth, well-balanced flavor with low acidity. Serve it well chilled over ice with a squeeze of lemon and a grind of black pepper. It is a great base for a Bloody Mary-style drink, a quick gazpacho, or a tomato rice, and a splash adds depth to soups and braises. The resealable bottle keeps it fresh in the fridge.",
  "tomato-juice-small-730236":
    "Our Italian tomato juice in a single-serve 6.76 oz size, made for one refreshing glass at a time. It has a smooth, savory tomato flavor that is best served cold, over ice, with a squeeze of lemon and a pinch of black pepper. Pack one in a lunchbox or a cooler, or keep a few in the fridge for a quick, savory drink in the afternoon. It is also a handy amount for a small batch of soup or rice.",
  "tomato-paste-tube":
    "A double-concentrated tomato paste made in Italy from Italian tomatoes, packed in a squeezable tube so you can use a spoonful at a time and keep the rest fresh. Sizzle a little in olive oil before adding the rest of your ingredients to build deep, rich tomato flavor in sauces, soups, stews, and braises. It also adds body to a quick pizza sauce or a pot of lentils. Recap and refrigerate after opening.",
  "tomato-puree":
    "Made in Italy from Italian tomatoes, our tomato puree is smooth and velvety, with a clean, sweet flavor. It is ready to become a quick pasta sauce: warm it with olive oil, garlic, and a few basil leaves for fifteen minutes. Use it as the base for a creamy tomato soup, a slow braise, or a pan of meatballs, and keep the opened bottle in the fridge.",
  "tomato-sauce-box":
    "Our passata is made in Italy from Italian tomatoes, strained into a smooth, pourable sauce with a clean, natural tomato flavor. The resealable screw-cap carton means you can use just what you need and save the rest in the fridge. Simmer it with olive oil, garlic, and basil for a quick pasta sauce, use it as the base for a tomato soup or a pot of braised chicken, or spread it on homemade pizza.",
  "tomato-savory-jam":
    "A savory tomato jam with a subtle sweetness, somewhere between a relish and a chutney. It is made in Italy from tomatoes and brings a rich, rounded flavor to cheese and crackers. Spread it on crostini with soft cheese, serve it alongside a cheese board or a plate of grilled meats, or spoon it onto a burger or a grilled cheese sandwich. It also makes a quick glaze for meatloaf or roasted chicken.",
  "traditional-pizza-sauce":
    "Our traditional pizza sauce is made in Italy from Italian tomatoes, seasoned with herbs and garlic for a classic pizzeria flavor. Its smooth, spreadable texture is ready straight from the jar, no cooking needed. Spread a thin layer over dough, top with mozzarella and basil, and bake hot for a homemade margherita. It is also great on English muffin pizzas, as a dip for mozzarella sticks, or spooned over baked eggplant.",
  "truffle-parchment-crackers-730333":
    "Paper-thin Italian parchment crackers with an earthy truffle aroma. They are light, crisp, and a little luxurious. Pair them with soft, mild cheeses, a mushroom spread, or a dollop of ricotta with honey, or simply enjoy them on their own with a glass of sparkling grape juice. They bring something special to any cheese board. Serve them in a tall glass so guests can break off a piece.",
  "truffle-parchment-crackers-small-730337":
    "Paper-thin parchment crackers made with olive oil and flavored with truffle. They have a delicate crunch and an earthy, savory aroma that feels a little special. Serve them with soft cheeses, a mushroom spread, or ricotta and honey, or enjoy them on their own. The 2.64 oz pack is perfect for an aperitivo for two.",
  "truffle-salt":
    "Mediterranean sea salt blended with Italian black truffle, bringing an earthy, savory truffle aroma to everyday food with a single pinch. Use it as a finishing salt, sprinkled on just before serving: over scrambled eggs, French fries, buttered pasta, a mushroom risotto, mashed potatoes, or a bowl of hot popcorn. A little goes a long way, so start light and add to taste.",
  "tuna-fillet-olive-oil-tall-jar":
    "Yellowfin tuna fillets packed in olive oil in a tall glass jar. The whole fillets are firm, moist, and full of deep, rich flavor, and they look beautiful on the table. Lift them out whole for an antipasto platter with roasted peppers, olives, and capers, lay them over a green salad, or toss large flakes with pasta, lemon zest, and parsley.",
  "tuna-salad-with-corn-beans-peppers-730455":
    "A ready-to-eat tuna salad with tuna mixed with corn, beans, and peppers. It is colorful, satisfying, and ready the moment you open it, with no chopping or mixing needed. Enjoy it straight from the pack for a quick lunch, spoon it over a bed of greens or cooked rice, or pile it onto toasted bread or crackers. It is a great one to keep at the office or pack for travel.",
  "tuna-solid-light-olive-oil-can":
    "Solid light yellowfin tuna packed in olive oil for a tender texture and a rich, delicate flavor. It is the pantry staple that turns into dinner in minutes. Mix it into pasta with cherry tomatoes and olives, build a niçoise-style salad with eggs, green beans, and potatoes, or make a classic tuna sandwich on ciabatta with a little lemon and black pepper.",
  "tuna-solid-light-water-can":
    "Solid light yellowfin tuna packed in water for a clean, delicate flavor and firm, tender pieces. Drain it and dress it your way: with mayonnaise, celery, and lemon for a classic tuna salad, with olive oil and herbs for a lighter Italian-style version, or flaked into a wrap, a grain bowl, or a pasta salad with vegetables.",
  "tuna-ventresca-olive-oil-tall-jar":
    "Ventresca is the tuna belly, a tender cut. Ours is yellowfin tuna belly packed in olive oil in a tall glass jar. It is silky, rich, and melts in your mouth. Serve it simply so it can shine: on toasted bread with a drizzle of the oil and a few capers, over a salad of white beans and red onion, or alongside sliced tomatoes and fresh basil.",
  "unpitted-olive-trio-trays-730085":
    "Three Italian olive varieties in a ready-to-serve tray, kept whole with their pits for the fullest flavor and firmest texture. It is a classic antipasto in one package: peel back the lid and set it out with crusty bread, cheese, and roasted peppers. Put a small dish nearby for the pits. These are especially good at room temperature, with a drizzle of olive oil and a little lemon zest over the top.",
  "vodka-sauce-730228":
    "A smooth, creamy tomato sauce in the classic pink vodka sauce style, made with dairy. It is ready to heat and toss with penne for penne alla vodka, or with rigatoni, gnocchi, or cheese ravioli. Warm it gently, add a splash of the pasta water to loosen it, and finish with grated cheese and a few basil leaves. It is also lovely in a baked pasta with mozzarella on top.",
  "white-cooking-wine":
    "Made in Italy from select grapes, our white cooking wine adds a clean, bright, aromatic note to everyday cooking. Pour a splash into a risotto after toasting the rice and let it absorb before adding stock. Use it to steam fish fillets with garlic and lemon, to deglaze a pan of sautéed chicken, or to lighten a cream sauce for pasta. Let it simmer for a minute or two so the flavor softens and blends in.",
  "white-wine-vinegar":
    "Made in Italy from white wine, this vinegar has a clean, crisp acidity and a subtle grape note that will not overpower delicate ingredients. Use it for light dressings over butter lettuce or fennel, in a quick beurre blanc for fish, or for pickling vegetables like cucumbers, carrots, and shallots. A splash brightens a potato salad or a pan sauce for chicken. Keep a bottle next to your olive oil for everyday cooking.",
  "whole-cherry-tomatoes":
    "Whole Italian cherry tomatoes, vine-ripened in rich volcanic soil and packed whole to keep their sweet, bright flavor and round shape. They burst gently as they cook, turning into a glossy, sweet sauce in minutes. Toss them into a hot pan with garlic and olive oil, then add spaghetti and basil for a quick pasta. They are also lovely baked with fish, spooned over bruschetta, or roasted alongside chicken.",
  "whole-peeled-tomatoes-large-730215":
    "Whole peeled Italian tomatoes in a large 28.2 oz size, for a big pot of Sunday sauce or a crowd-sized lasagna. They are packed whole at peak ripeness, so they keep their sweet, vibrant flavor. Crush them by hand into warm olive oil and garlic, add basil, and let them simmer low until thick. Blend them smooth for a silky soup, or slow-cook them with onions and meatballs for a rich ragù.",
  "zesty-marinara-sauce":
    "Our marinara with a little extra spirit: ripe Italian tomatoes simmered with garlic, herbs, and a gentle kick of red pepper. It is bold and lively without being fiery. Toss it with penne for a quick arrabbiata-style dinner, spoon it over eggplant parmigiana, or use it as a pizza sauce when you want some heat. It also wakes up meatballs, baked fish, and a skillet of shakshuka.",
};
